{
  "_notes": [
    "Spider-Man V2.61 (sman_261). Upstream had no map for any non-VE Spider-Man set.",
    "NVRAM fields were read from the ROM image by backport tools/samrom/samrom.py (adjustment records,",
    "the high-score descriptor table, the Master Volume setter, the score array literal), the rules",
    "validated on the mapped SAM games. Only sman_261 is claimed: sman_250, sman_260 and sman_262 were",
    "not available to check, and sman_240 and earlier move the scores, the volume and the records.",
    "Free Play is record 33 (ROM adjustment ID 34), Balls Per Game 30, Credit Limit 32: the offset-0 layout.",
    "Champion records are the 36-byte form: checksum16 at +32, the score a 64-bit integer at +24.",
    "A saved sman_261 NVRAM from an ALP4K cabinet validates all twelve records that way (and none with",
    "the checksum at +28), the three adjustments and Master Volume (40, check byte 215).",
    "Mode champions follow smanve_101: Combo Champion (factory 20) and Spider Champion (25) hold counts",
    "and Best Combo Champion a one-byte count at +0x1A (5), declared as counter; Spider Sense, Battle",
    "Royale, Super Hero and Best Bonus hold scores.",
    "current_player and current_ball are adjacent at 0x000365D4/0x000365D5: the ROM offers this and",
    "0x0003FCFF, and a headless libpinmame run (two players, two tilts) found only this one.",
    "Status byte 0x00036606 (player + 0x32): 01 in attract, 13 with a ball in play, 15 from each tilt to",
    "the next ball -- the variant that keeps bit 0x01 in play, as on st_161h. game_over is any bit",
    "above 0x01 (mask 0xFE inverted); tilted is an enum over mask 0x1F with only 21 (0x15) true.",
    "Confirmed on an ALP4K cabinet (2026-11-11): a two-player game tilted on P1's ball 1. ScoreServer",
    "decoded both final scores exactly (2,081,890 and 1,757,670), all twelve champion records, and ended",
    "the game on game_over when the status byte returned to 01 after P2's last ball, which the headless",
    "run never reached. The status byte read 15 only for the tilted ball; no other in-game value appeared.",
    "Scores are 4 bytes on 8-byte centres from 0x02110A24.",
    "Master Volume 0x02110250, 0-63, factory 40, complement check byte after it."
  ],
